        {
          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Owner metadata reconciliation for Definition(ii): restricting the upper semicontinuous pairs (inv,nu) and (inv,rho) to a primary level {inv=a} gives the relative auxiliary superlevels. This proves the stated forward implication. The finite-range primary hypothesis makes the level strata locally closed; the explicit finite-stratum argument is supplied in Proposition proof 6.1.",
          "attribution": "Owner local metadata reconciliation, not a native or independent rereview."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-reverse",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Owner metadata reconciliation for Definition(ii): if inv has finite range and closed superlevels, and an auxiliary superlevel F is closed on {inv=a}, its closure lies in {inv>=a} and meets {inv=a} exactly in F. Hence {inv>a} union F is closed and is the lexicographic pair superlevel. This proves the stated reverse implication for each auxiliary function; standalone auxiliary USC is not inferred.",
          "attribution": "Owner local metadata reconciliation, not a native or independent rereview."
        }
      ]
    },
